# `src-tauri/tests/bindings_contract.rs` compares the checked-in bindings byte
# for byte against what specta generates, and specta always emits LF. A checkout
# that converted either side to CRLF — `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows — would
# fail that test on every line rather than on drift, which reads as a broken gate
# rather than a platform difference. Pin the two files the comparison touches.
src/lib/bindings.ts text eol=lf
src-tauri/bindings-header.txt text eol=lf
